{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":881,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.144","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 144","reference":"Psalms 144","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"David blesses God for his mercies, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-4.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"Prays against his enemies, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"5-8.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"Promises to praise him, ver.9-11.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"The happiness of those who serve God, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"12-15.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":8,"text":"A psalm of David.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":9,"text":"2.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":10,"text":"Subdued - Who hath disposed my peoples hearts to receive and obey me as their king.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":11,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":12,"text":"Come - To help me.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":13,"text":"Smoke - As Sinai did at thy glorious appearance, Exod. xix, 18.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":14,"text":"This is a figurative and poetical description of God's coming to take vengeance upon his enemies.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":15,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":16,"text":"Strange children - Either of the Heathen nations: or of the rebellious Israelites.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":17,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":18,"text":"Vanity - Vain brags and threatenings which shall come to nothing.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":19,"text":"Falsehood - Deceiving themselves, by being unable to do what they designed; and others, by not giving them that help which they promised.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":20,"text":"12.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":21,"text":"That - This mercy I beg not only for my own sake, but for the sake of thy people, that they may enjoy those blessings which thou hast promised them; and particularly, that our sons, who are the strength and hopes of a nation, may be like plants, flourishing and growing in height and strength, as plants do in their youth; for when they grow old, they wither and decay.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":22,"text":"Cornerstone - Strong and beautiful.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":23,"text":"14.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":24,"text":"Breaking in - Of enemies invading the land, or assaulting our cities, and making breaches in their walls.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":25,"text":"Going out - Of our people, either out of the cities to fight with an invading enemy: or out of the land into captivity.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":144}}